<course_map memo="based on syllabus">
Week blocks (SW chapters):
1) Review probability & stats (SW 1–3) → foundations, sampling, confidence.
2) Bivariate OLS (SW 4–5) → slope meaning, bias sources, sampling distribution.
3) Multiple OLS (SW 6–7) → controls, omitted variable bias, multicollinearity, functional form.
4) Nonlinear models (SW 8) → logs, polynomials, interactions, elasticities.
5) Assessing regression studies (SW 9) → threats to internal/external validity, design critique.
6) Panel data (SW 10) → FE/RE, within estimator, assumptions.
7) Binary dependent variables (SW 11) → LPM vs logit/probit, interpretation.
8) Instrumental variables (SW 12) → relevance/exclusion, 2SLS, weak‑IV tests.
9) Experiments (SW 13) → randomization inference, noncompliance (ITT/LATE), power.
10) Many predictors & big data (SW 14) → high‑level model selection ideas.
11) Time series (SW 15–16) → stationarity, AR(p), ARMA, forecasting, serial correlation.
</course_map>

