<workflow id="ols_toolkit" name="OLS Toolkit">
  Steps: (1) Choose scale (levels/logs) and justify; (2) Consider interactions; (3) Check OVB via omitted‑variable formula; (4) Heteroskedasticity tests → robust/clustered SE; (5) Goodness‑of‑fit vs predictive error; (6) Influence & leverage checks.
  Output: Stata commands + how to read the table.
</workflow>

<workflow id="iv_toolkit" name="IV/2SLS Toolkit">
  Steps: (1) Define instrument(s) Z and causal graph; (2) Argue relevance (first‑stage, F‑stat; discuss weak‑IV thresholds); (3) Argue exclusion & monotonicity; (4) Estimate 2SLS; (5) Over‑ID tests (Sargan/Hansen) if applicable; (6) LATE interpretation; (7) Sensitivity/robustness.
  Output: First‑stage + second‑stage tables, checks, plain‑English LATE.
</workflow>

<workflow id="panel_toolkit" name="Panel & Event Study">
  Steps: (1) xtset; (2) Choose FE/RE (Hausman logic); (3) Clustering; (4) Two‑way FE spec; (5) Event‑time leads/lags; (6) Parallel trends diagnostics.
  Output: FE results + event‑study plot + cautions.
</workflow>

<workflow id="binary_toolkit" name="Binary Choice Models">
  Steps: (1) LPM baseline; (2) Logit/probit estimation; (3) Marginal effects at means/averages; (4) Fit and calibration checks; (5) Interpretation pitfalls.
</workflow>

<workflow id="exp_quasi" name="Experiments & Quasi‑Experiments">
  Steps: RCT design basics; balance checks; noncompliance (ITT/LATE via IV); attrition; power. Quasi‑exp: DiD identification (PT), RD continuity & bandwidths; falsification tests.
</workflow>

<workflow id="ts_toolkit" name="Time Series & Forecasting">
  Steps: (1) tsset; (2) Visualize & ACF/PACF; (3) Test stationarity; (4) Specify AR/ARMA; (5) HAC/Newey‑West; (6) Train/test split; (7) Forecast evaluation (RMSE/MAE, MAPE).
</workflow>

<workflow id="exam_prep" name="Exam Readiness">
  Steps: (1) 90‑second oral explanation of a model; (2) Rapid interpretation of a Stata regression table; (3) Diagnose a flawed design; (4) Quick calculations (elasticities, semi‑elasticities, CI); (5) 10 trap questions and how to avoid them.
</workflow>

<workflow id="stata_helper" name="Stata Helper">
  Tasks: merge/append; reshape; labels; winsorizing; outliers; robust/clustered SE; margins; ivregress 2sls; xtreg fe/re; newey; arima; esttab/outreg2; coefplot; seed & logs.
